# Git rewrites line endings on checkout unless told otherwise, and on Windows
# that means every Go file arrives CRLF and gofmt reports the whole tree as
# unformatted — burying real formatting drift in noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# One EOL rewrite inside these corrupts them outright; never let git touch
# their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpeg binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.exe binary

# Lockfiles are text, but their hashes churn if line endings wobble between
# machines; pinning them keeps diffs reviewable and installs reproducible.
package-lock.json text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
